<p>The U.S. military said all six crew members aboard an Air Force KC-135 refueling aircraft died when the plane crashed in western Iraq. U.S. Central Command said hostile fire and friendly fire did not cause the loss, and investigators are still working to determine what happened. Several reports said the Islamic Resistance in Iraq claimed it had shot down the aircraft. But U.S. military statements cited in those same reports said the crash was not caused by hostile action.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JaEpoACyMQDtsHvAhhLQ9pFkEzTyeIWu8C3fWoiEo_G3UKSwIVFWIS7gN1fsHjTAHJDURGozzV3M7CgopAm-I6JxYgGK3_bed9_0_x9ORZ_d' alt='A US Air Force KC-135 aerial refueling aircraft is seen at Riga International Airport, Latvia June 6, 2018.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Wider toll: The six deaths bring the number of U.S. service members killed in the Iran war to at least 13, after seven earlier fatalities since operations began.</li><li>Air buildup: Dawn reported that the United States has sent a large number of aircraft into the Middle East for the war, underscoring that the tanker was part of a much broader regional air campaign.</li><li>Second aircraft: A U.S. official cited by Reuters in Dawn said the other aircraft involved was also a KC-135 refueling plane and landed safely.</li></ul><blockquote>War is hell. War is chaos, and as we saw yesterday with the tragic crash of our KC-135 tanker, bad things can happen - Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Central Command: CENTCOM said investigators are examining the crash and that hostile fire and friendly fire did not bring down the aircraft. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-refuelling-tanker-crash-iraq-crew-dead-war-march-13-2026/article70738848.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Islamic Resistance in Iraq: The loose alliance of Iran-backed Iraqi factions claimed it had downed a KC-135 and had also targeted another plane that escaped, according to reports citing the claim. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-refuelling-tanker-crash-iraq-crew-dead-war-march-13-2026/article70738848.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-refuelling-tanker-crash-iraq-crew-dead-war-march-13-2026/article70738848.ece'>All six service members killed in plane crash in Iraq, says U.S. military</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-war-kc-135-us-plane-crash-iraq-crew-deaths-confirmed/'>All 6 crew members killed in crash of U.S. KC-135 refueling aircraft in Iraq</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981530/six-us-service-members-killed-in-plane-crash-over-iraq'>Six US service members killed in plane crash over Iraq</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/12/world/middleeast/us-refueling-plane-crash-iraq.html'>All 6 Crew Members Killed in U.S. Refueling Plane Crash in Iraq, Military Says</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/all-six-crew-members-aboard-refueling-aircraft-killed-in-crash-in-iraq-says-us-military-ws-e-13989360.html'>All six crew members aboard refueling aircraft killed in crash in Iraq, says US military</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/us-raises-death-toll-from-refueling-aircraft-crash-from-four-to-six/'>The United States military confirms that all six crew members aboard an Air Force Boeing KC-135 Stratotanker died when the aircraft crashed in western Iraq yesterday.</a> - timesofisrael.com</li></ul>